{"query":"Search for the original uploader and earliest dated copy of the specific video, using reverse video/keyframe search and archive records, to establish its provenance and first publication date.","results":[{"date":"Sep 10, 2026","position":1,"site_name":"somiq.veriqlabs.com","snippet":"Learn how to reverse search a video using keyframes, screenshots, search engines, timestamps, and source tracing to find its original source and context.","title":"How to Reverse Search a Video and Find Its Original Source ...","url":"https://somiq.veriqlabs.com/blog/how-to-reverse-search-a-video-and-find-where-it-originally-came-from"},{"date":"Oct 8, 2026","position":2,"site_name":"maxintel.org","snippet":"How to verify a video step by step in 2026: C2PA Content Credentials, SynthID and Sora watermarks, InVID keyframes, metadata, forensics and a 12-step workflow.","title":"How to Verify a Video in 2026: Provenance, Frames, Deepfakes","url":"https://maxintel.org/video-verification-guide-2026.html"},{"date":"Aug 14, 2026","position":3,"site_name":"deepsearch.app","snippet":"Preserve the copy and its page context, search the whole image plus distinctive crops or video keyframes, then build a dated candidate timeline. Follow credits and links backward until they reach a creator or attributable publication. Report the result as a confirmed creator publication, earliest public copy located, likely source, or unresolved, because the oldest indexed result is not ...","title":"How to find the original source of a photo or video","url":"https://deepsearch.app/guides/how-to-find-the-original-source-of-a-photo-or-video"},{"position":4,"site_name":"reverse-video-search.app","snippet":"Find who posted a video first: search its frames to find every copy, compare upload dates and open the earliest one. Works with TikTok and YouTube links. Free.","title":"Who Posted This Video First? Find the Original Uploader","url":"https://reverse-video-search.app/who-posted-this-video-first/"},{"position":5,"site_name":"reversevideosearch.co","snippet":"Upload a video, paste a public URL, or search by keywords to find matching pages and investigate original video sources with Reverse Video Search.","title":"Reverse Video Search: Upload a Clip or Paste a URL","url":"https://reversevideosearch.co/"},{"position":6,"site_name":"www.reversevideosearch.io","snippet":"A video reverse search engine helps you find where a video appears online by analyzing its visual content instead of relying on titles or descriptions. It works like a pipeline for extracting keyframes from a clip and comparing them against publicly indexed images and thumbnails across the web.","title":"Reverse Video Search","url":"https://www.reversevideosearch.io/"},{"date":"Feb 17, 2026","position":7,"site_name":"detectvideo.ai","snippet":"Reverse video search is the process of tracing a video back to its earliest available source, a longer version, or the original context in which it appeared. If you have a short clip, a repost, a social media link, or even one clear frame, you can often find the original video by combining keyframe search, visual search, exact-text queries ...","title":"Reverse Video Search: Find the Original Video Source","url":"https://detectvideo.ai/reverse-video-search/"}],"total_results":7,"page":0}